A security baseline establishes minimum security requirements that Azure workloads should meet before being considered production-ready.

A baseline can include:

* Microsoft Entra ID authentication
* MFA
* Least-privilege RBAC
* Network segmentation
* NSGs
* Encryption
* Key management
* Logging
* Security monitoring
* Backup and recovery

For example, an organization can require all privileged administrator accounts to use MFA and all production workloads to follow predefined network security standards.

A real-life use case is a financial organization applying a common security baseline across multiple Azure subscriptions.

Security baselines reduce configuration inconsistencies and establish a minimum acceptable security posture.
